OL,3,GNEWSAPC denies confrontation with care
OL,4,Ahome amputee
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen asked if he should have tried to
OL,7,Festablish a rapport with Donald
OL,8,FBurgess, who had dementia, Smith
OL,9,Freplied "no".
OL,11,F"All he had to do was listen to my
OL,12,Ffirst verbal command," added Smith, who
OL,13,Falso used his baton on the wheelchair
OL,14,Fuser.
